## Delegating work to the cloud agent (MCP server "delegate")

Use `delegate_task` for self-contained work that can run unattended in a sandbox (long refactors,
test fixing, data processing, research that produces files). The cloud agent cannot see this machine
and cannot ask questions, so:

1. Write a complete brief: goal, context, constraints, acceptance criteria, how to verify.
2. Inputs: for a project, call `create_upload`, then run the printed command in the project root, e.g.
   `git ls-files -co --exclude-standard -z | tar --null -T - -czf - | curl -fsS -T - '<upload_url>'`,
   and pass the upload id to `delegate_task(upload_ids=[...])`. Never paste file contents into tool
   arguments except for tiny snippets.
3. While the result says the task is still running, call `wait_task(task_id=...)` again.
4. Review the report, then apply the patch from the project root with the printed
   `curl ... && git apply ...` command; fetch output files the same way.
